<title>GERMANY: East German Oct industrial orders fall 3.0 pct.</title>
<headline>East German Oct industrial orders fall 3.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Oct 96    Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   -3.0	 -2.0	+14.0</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     -10.3	 +5.3	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		126.6	130.5	141.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				  Oct 96   Sept 96    Oct 96 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     -1.9	 -2.6     148.5</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Sept/Oct 96 with Jul/Aug 96:  Manufacturing orders		  -5.5</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Sept/Oct 96 with Sept/Oct 95:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  -1.3</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 -1.9</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +2.1</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +12.7</p>
<p> Capital goods			  -20.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +7.2</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
